Adapt Jesvi-iOS's RedwoodMetal driver (userland/src, MIT) to the Galaxy A8 2018 port.

- the GPU service: JackpotlteMali (xnu 0154) first. Its requests are panfrost's
  (0x42 CREATE_BO with the GPU address back, 0x44 GET_PARAM, 0x09 GEM_CLOSE,
  IOConnectMapMemory64 with the handle as the memory type) = Jesvi's RedwoodMali
  shape, so gpu_is_mali is set for it; RedwoodGPU / RedwoodMali stay as fallbacks.
- the drawable's surface request 0x7e: same number; JackpotlteMali takes the first
  40 bytes of struct rwd_surface and hands back what it was given (planeOffset /
  planeRowBytes come back zero: one plane).
- the compiler library: /private/var/mobile/Library/a8air/libredwoodair.dylib (P13
  phase 2's path; a copy beside the bundle's executable still wins).
- class JackpotlteMetalDevice (a subclass, nothing added): the MetalPluginClassName
  our kernel's jtmetal=1 and the fix library's per-process hook name.
- metal_props: our names, and a note that our accelerator takes no properties.
featureProfile stays Jesvi's default 1 (metal_profile= boot-arg to change).

